            <ArticleTitle>[Dissecting aortic aneurysm complicated by rupture of the right coronary artery and acute myocardial infarction--in a person treated with fibrinolysis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case report of 45-year-old woman with acute inferior wall and right ventricle myocardial infarction treated with i.v. Streptokinase is presented. Few days later acute aortic dissection involving right coronary artery was detected. After six days the patient was successfully operated. She is in good condition 10 months afterwards.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
